       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Safety:** The dose is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum of 2,550 mg/day. That risk is the same whoever confirms it.\n- **Authority:** You've told me you're the CEO and not a clinician. A confirmation from you isn't a prescriber's authorization. The order needs to come from the patient's treating physician, NP, or PA.\n\n**Options:**\n- The treating prescriber can tell me the dose they intend, and I'll enter it if it's within the safe range. For example, 850 mg three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day.\n- If the prescriber really intends a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves. They should also talk with pharmacy, so it goes through the hospital's override and verification process.\n\nIf you tell me the prescriber's intended dose, I can enter the order right away."
